          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Intuitively speaking, a braided monoidal category is a category with a tensor product and an isomorphism called the ‘braiding’ which lets us ‘switch’ two objects in a tensor product like
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes y
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
          %p
            A braided monoidal category is a special case of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+pseudomonoid"} braided pseudomonoid
            in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+2-category"} braided monoidal 2-category
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #BraidedMonoidalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %strong braided monoidal category
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
