            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
              , Section 2:
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#BasicNotionsOfCategoricalAlgebra"} Basic notions of categorical algebra
          %p
            The original articles on braided monoidal categories (the published version does not completely supersede the
            = succeed "," do
              %em Macquarie Math Reports
          %ul
            %li#JoyalStreet85
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braided monoidal categories
                %em Macquarie Math Reports
                %strong 85-0067
                (1985) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://web.science.mq.edu.au/~street/BMC850067.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalStreet-BraidedMonoidal85.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#JoyalStreet86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braided monoidal categories
                %em Macquarie Math Reports
                %strong 86-0081
                (1986) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://maths.mq.edu.au/~street/JS1.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalStreet-BraidedMonoidal.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braided tensor categories
                %strong 102
                (1993) 20-78 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.1993.1055"}> doi:10.1006/aima.1993.1055
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Around the same time the same definition was also proposed independently by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawrence+Breen"} Lawrence Breen
            in a letter to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"} Pierre Deligne
          %ul
            %li#Breen88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawrence+Breen"}> Lawrence Breen
              ,
              %em
                Une lettre à P. Deligne au sujet des
                = succeed "-cat\u00E9gories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              (1988) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-paris13.fr/~breen/deligne.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Exposition of basic definitions:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/qg-fall2004/definitions.pdf"} Some definitions everyone should know
              (2004)
          %p
            An elementary introduction using
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
          %ul
            %li#BaezStay11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"} Mike Stay
              = succeed "," do
                %em Physics, Topology, Logic and Computation: A Rosetta Stone
              = succeed "," do
                %em New Structures for Physics
              %strong 813
              Springer (2011) 95-174 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.0340"}> arXiv:0903.0340
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-12821-9_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-12821-9_2
          %p
            A generalisation of braidings to
            %em lax braidings
            (called
            %em pre-braidings
            by Yetter), where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is not required to be invertible:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Yetter"}> David Yetter
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum groups and representations of monoidal categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"}> Brian Day
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elango+Panchadcharam"} Elango Panchadcharam
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lax braidings and the lax centre
